  "id": "computational-metaphor",
  "term": "computational metaphor",
  "definition": "The computational metaphor is the view of mind as a closed system that processes symbols in a linear way. In this learning context, it refers to a traditional cognitivist model that is criticized as too limited for explaining complex, real-time, emotionally and socially shaped learning in dynamic situations.",
